	Functions in Oracle Database
		- Oracle Funtions are predefined routines that take input values, and perform an operation and retur
		- In a simple words, Funtion return a value
		- They can be used in SELECT, WHERE, ORDER BY, GROUP BY and HAVING and many other SQL opertaions.
		- Funtions fall into two major categories:
		
	1. Single RoW(Scalar) Funtions
		- These functions operte on one row at a time and return one value per row.
	Types:
		- String Functions
		- UPPER/LOWER/INITCAP
		- Numeric Functions
		- Date Functions
		- Conversion Functions
		- Conditional Functions
		- General Functions

	2. Multiple-Row (Aggregate) Functions
		- These functions operate on group of rows and return one result per group
	Types:
		- SUM
		- COUNT
		- AVG
		- MAX/MIN
		- STDDEV
		
	Note:  Function always returns a only one value.
	
